{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RrxRULAuLn8Y19oCmSHFdj","type":"tool_result","content":"596\t\n597\tThat second half is an observation, not a documented claim. Hold the two apart: *launched automatically where the addon manager runs* is sourced; *practically universal* is the author's report.\n598\t\n599\tWhich brings us to the sentence this section exists for.\n600\t\n601\t> ⚓ **Worth Securing — the absent-component pattern.** An object can exist while nothing at all happens, if the component that would act on it is absent. The object is real; it's stored; `kubectl get` will show it to you. But an object is a *description*, and descriptions don't do anything by themselves. Something has to be watching for it and willing to act. Remember the phrase: **an object without its component does nothing.** You're going to meet it four more times in this book, and each time it will look like a completely different problem until you recognize it.\n602\t\n603\t*[cross-bearing: see Ch 9 — CoreDNS as the cluster DNS addon, and the Service DNS records it serves]*\n604\t*[cross-bearing: see Ch 10 — an Ingress with no Ingress controller does nothing at all: the same pattern, first recurrence]*\n605\t*[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 — `kubectl top` with no metrics-server installed]*\n606\t*[cross-bearing: see Ch 17 — VPA is an addon and is not shipped by default]*\n607\t\n608\t---\n609\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"737bec61-26cb-41a1-9e4d-42094b6c400b","uuid":"2f2cb2bd-5fb1-49bc-ade3-f8d23332a8ab","timestamp":"2026-08-25T03:31:37.025Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\chapter-03-the-ship-s-company.md","content":"\nThat second half is an observation, not a documented claim. Hold the two apart: *launched automatically where the addon manager runs* is sourced; *practically universal* is the author's report.\n\nWhich brings us to the sentence this section exists for.\n\n> ⚓ **Worth Securing — the absent-component pattern.** An object can exist while nothing at all happens, if the component that would act on it is absent. The object is real; it's stored; `kubectl get` will show it to you. But an object is a *description*, and descriptions don't do anything by themselves. Something has to be watching for it and willing to act. Remember the phrase: **an object without its component does nothing.** You're going to meet it four more times in this book, and each time it will look like a completely different problem until you recognize it.\n\n*[cross-bearing: see Ch 9 — CoreDNS as the cluster DNS addon, and the Service DNS records it serves]*\n*[cross-bearing: see Ch 10 — an Ingress with no Ingress controller does nothing at all: the same pattern, first recurrence]*\n*[cross-bearing: see Ch 13 — `kubectl top` with no metrics-server installed]*\n*[cross-bearing: see Ch 17 — VPA is an addon and is not shipped by default]*\n\n---\n","numLines":14,"startLine":596,"totalLines":1322}}}
